Mineralogy — Dexter Perkins, open editions (@mp-mineralogy: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_3Y3EJ93EG4V7Q0TZBCRRXVNVKP
Dexter Perkins. Mineralogy. University of North Dakota, 2020 open-textbook deposit, DOI 10.31356/oers025. [Author's institutional edition and downloads](https://commons.und.edu/oers/20/) · [University of Tennessee at Chattanooga online edition](https://utc.pressbooks.pub/mineralogy/) · [Author's maintained edition](https://opengeology.org/Mineralogy/).

Read the whole book with examples, exercises, and descriptive mineral references. Its sequence connects chemistry, properties, crystallization, optics, mineral/rock groups, morphology/symmetry, crystallography, and diffraction/analysis. Use topic names and the actual edition where numbering differs. The October 2020 repository file is explicitly a beta snapshot; do not silently treat it as the latest maintained edition.

The institutional record states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Preserve actual edition/component credits. The UTC contents and some chapters were accessible, with later requests returning 403; the maintained host uses a browser challenge. Access and bibliographic distinctions checked on 29 October 2026. Books and media are external links only.

